{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FeK52pCfs5ieKdpVXgh9x4","type":"tool_result","content":"111:## Merge close-gate (#387)\n112-\n113-The closing-keyword rule above wires the auto-close; this gate governs **when a PR carrying one may\n114-merge**. They are separate concerns: a keyword makes the merge *close* the issue, the close-gate\n115-makes sure the issue is *actually done* before that happens.\n116-\n117-The machine convention is intentionally narrow:\n118-\n119-- A **close-gated PR** is any PR whose body contains a GitHub closing keyword for an issue:\n120-  `Closes #N`, `Fixes #N`, or `Resolves #N` (including `closed`/`fixed`/`resolved` variants and full\n121-  GitHub issue URLs).\n122-- A **close-gated issue checkbox** is either:\n123-  - any markdown checkbox inside an issue section whose heading contains `acceptance`, `definition\n124-    of done`, `gate`, or `fitness gate`; or\n125-  - any markdown checkbox anywhere in the issue body whose checkbox text starts with `gate:`.\n126-- Ordinary planning, dependency, sub-issue, or rollout checklists outside those sections are **not**\n127-  close-gated. If a checklist is acceptance, put it under an acceptance/gate heading.\n128-- Only markdown checkboxes are close-gated and mirrorable. A plain-bullet `Acceptance` section has\n129-  no mirrorable targets and therefore takes no `acceptance-evidence` block; convert its bullets to\n130-  markdown checkboxes before adding a block.\n131-- A checked acceptance/gate box must carry linked evidence in the issue, PR body, or PR phase comment\n132-  (command output, run URL, CI job, or reviewer/evaluator comment). The automation catches unchecked\n133-  boxes; the coordinator/evaluator verifies the evidence link quality before closing.\n134-\n135-For the normal evidence-mirroring path, put one fenced `acceptance-evidence` YAML block in the PR\n136-body or a PR comment for each closing issue. Map each unchecked box by exact text after 