{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qx34mWTCxd3YE74zEDXDZ6","type":"tool_result","content":"104:## 5. Implement\n105-\n106-1. Implement one commit slice at a time in the Design order.\n107-2. After each slice:\n108-   - run the slice's named gate,\n109-   - **Slice review gate (Amendment A1)** — before the sign-off commit, the Tier-A supervisor\n110-     substantively reviews the landed slice (correctness, coherence with already-landed slices,\n111-     doctrine-fit, gaps/overreach). No implementation lane (Tier B/C/D) self-certifies; passing\n112-     automated gates is not a sign-off. See `workflow/lane-policy.md` §\"Slice review gate (Amendment\n113-     A1)\" for the lane-agnostic invariant this step enforces.\n114-   - commit (the **sign-off commit**, the supervisor's) with a message that names what the slice\n115-     proves, not what it contains,\n116-   - push, then comment on the draft PR with the slice scope, commit hash, and gate evidence — the\n117-     draft-PR commit list + per-slice PR comments are the commit trail (there is no `commits.md`),\n118-   - update `worklog.md` + `context-pack.md` as part of the same slice (a slice whose commit does\n119-     not touch the run dir is incomplete),\n120-   - run the **post-slice reconcile loop** (below) and write one reconcile note in `worklog.md`.\n121-3. Append `drift.md` when facts diverge from the plan, RFC, or doctrine.\n122-\n123-Before committing, inspect `git status --short` and do not fold in unrelated user changes. If an\n124-unrelated change shares a file you must edit, work with the current content instead of reverting it.\n125-\n126:### Concept of Done (per slice)\n127-\n128-A slice is done when:\n129-\n130-- every file in the slice is reachable from the public surface or a test,\n131-- no file exists to satisfy a folder shape without being used,\n132-- constants replace string literals for finite domain vocabularies,\n133-- public functions have a JSDoc one-liner (what it does, not how),\n134-- a contributor can extend the slice by reading one file and copying a pattern,\n135-- the slice's gate passes.\n136-\n137-### Post-slice reconcile loop\n138-\n139-After each slice completes (and before starting the next), reconcile the GitHub surface with the\n140-run:\n141-\n142-1. **Sweep related issues** — check their state, any needed `status:`/`area:`/milestone moves, and\n143-   that the resolving PR carries the right closing keyword (`Closes #N` for full resolution, a bare\n144-   reference for partial work — see `netscript-pr`).\n145-2. **Read new issue/PR comments** since the last sweep (evaluator verdicts, reviewer notes,\n146-   OpenHands output).\n147-3. **Record readjustments** — fold plan changes into `plan.md`; append `drift.md` when reality\n148-   diverged from the plan or doctrine.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c74d687f-4c79-4f44-a79b-d844085dc27a","uuid":"3b3eddde-394b-4f2a-be7f-2f13e3c7d46d","timestamp":"2026-09-03T02:22:13.847Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"104:## 5. Implement\n105-\n106-1. Implement one commit slice at a time in the Design order.\n107-2. After each slice:\n108-   - run the slice's named gate,\n109-   - **Slice review gate (Amendment A1)** — before the sign-off commit, the Tier-A supervisor\n110-     substantively reviews the landed slice (correctness, coherence with already-landed slices,\n111-     doctrine-fit, gaps/overreach). No implementation lane (Tier B/C/D) self-certifies; passing\n112-     automated gates is not a sign-off. See `workflow/lane-policy.md` §\"Slice review gate (Amendment\n113-     A1)\" for the lane-agnostic invariant this step enforces.\n114-   - commit (the **sign-off commit**, the supervisor's) with a message that names what the slice\n115-     proves, not what it contains,\n116-   - push, then comment on the draft PR with the slice scope, commit hash, and gate evidence — the\n117-     draft-PR commit list + per-slice PR comments are the commit trail (there is no `commits.md`),\n118-   - update `worklog.md` + `context-pack.md` as part of the same slice (a slice whose commit does\n119-     not touch the run dir is incomplete),\n120-   - run the **post-slice reconcile loop** (below) and write one reconcile note in `worklog.md`.\n121-3. Append `drift.md` when facts diverge from the plan, RFC, or doctrine.\n122-\n123-Before committing, inspect `git status --short` and do not fold in unrelated user changes. If an\n124-unrelated change shares a file you must edit, work with the current content instead of reverting it.\n125-\n126:### Concept of Done (per slice)\n127-\n128-A slice is done when:\n129-\n130-- every file in the slice is reachable from the public surface or a test,\n131-- no file exists to satisfy a folder shape without being used,\n132-- constants replace string literals for finite domain vocabularies,\n133-- public functions have a JSDoc one-liner (what it does, not how),\n134-- a contributor can extend the slice by reading one file and copying a pattern,\n135-- the slice's gate passes.\n136-\n137-### Post-slice reconcile loop\n138-\n139-After each slice completes (and before starting the next), reconcile the GitHub surface with the\n140-run:\n141-\n142-1. **Sweep related issues** — check their state, any needed `status:`/`area:`/milestone moves, and\n143-   that the resolving PR carries the right closing keyword (`Closes #N` for full resolution, a bare\n144-   reference for partial work — see `netscript-pr`).\n145-2. **Read new issue/PR comments** since the last sweep (evaluator verdicts, reviewer notes,\n146-   OpenHands output).\n147-3. **Record readjustments** — fold plan changes into `plan.md`; append `drift.md` when reality\n148-   diverged from the plan or doctrine.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
